  "claim_scope": "GT-1 Mamba-2/SSD implementation contract: the learner implements stable segment sums, a semiseparable matrix, independent recurrent and quadratic SSD forms, chunked SSD, grouped multi-head parameters, a gated residual block, and exact convolution/SSM cache decoding, a stacked LM, and runnable parameter-matched attention and Mamba-1 controls. Float64 outputs, final states, and gradients agree with the literal recurrence and the official repository's SSD Listing 1. A trained tiny Mamba-2 mixer solves generated delayed recall while recurrent-state ablation, a finite local convolution, and shuffled-label training remain near chance. All 219 tensors from pinned Mamba-2 130M map strictly into a faithful from-scratch 24-layer LM; 25 hidden states, logits, and top tokens match Transformers on two prompts. The strict CUDA release hook additionally compares against the official fused SSD kernel. The paper's optimized training-speed claim is not reproduced.",
